<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch cocoa grind up 3.90 pct yr/yr in Q4 1996.</title>
<headline>Dutch cocoa grind up 3.90 pct yr/yr in Q4 1996.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dutch cocoa grind rose 3.90 percent to 97,273 tonnes in the fourth quarter of 1996 from 93,619 tonnes in the same 1995 period, the Dutch Cocoa Association (NCV) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The fourth quarter figure gives a full-year 1996 total of 388,412 tonnes, up 9.26 percent from 1995's 355,492 tonnes.</p>
<p>Analysts and industry sources said they had expected the fourth quarter grind to rise by around five percent.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
